        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Launches Lockdown Mode to Prevent Data Exfiltration\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released Lockdown Mode to help prevent the final stage of data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. This directly addresses the 'Lethal Trifecta' (private data access + untrusted content exposure + data exfiltration vectors) by cutting off the exfiltration leg. Simon Willison notes this implies ChatGPT's default settings don't provide robust protection against determined data exfiltration attacks.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-05\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"prompt-injection\", \"data-exfiltration\", \"llms\", \"openai\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"AI Enthusiasts vs. Skeptics: Race Against Time vs. Entropy\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"Charity Majors captures the dynamic between AI enthusiasts and skeptics: enthusiasts race against time as teams that don't adopt AI could face existential threats from competitors, while skeptics race against entropy as shipping code faster than engineers can read degrades reliability and institutional knowledge. The key issue is there's no natural feedback loop connecting the two groups.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Charity Majors)\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-skeptics/\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"ai\", \"engineering-culture\", \"organizational-design\", \"agentic-engineering\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    21→  }\n    22→]\n    23→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
